      preset={walkPreset}\n  949 |           activeIndex={walkActiveIndex}\n> 950 |           dataUrlByIndex={walkDataRef.current}\n      |                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  951 |           onSelectCell={selectWalkCell}\n  952 |           onChangePreset={handleChangeWalkPreset}\n  953 |           onionSkin={onionSkin}","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\DrawingEditor.tsx:62:3\n  60 |   const [onionSkinOpacity, setOnionSkinOpacity] = useState(20);\n  61 |\n> 62 |   toolRef.current = tool;\n     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot update ref during render\n  63 |   colorRef.current = color;\n  64 |\n  65 |   const currentSize = tool === 'brush' ? brushSize : tool === 'eraser' ? eraserSize : penSize;","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\DrawingEditor.tsx:63:3\n  61 |\n  62 |   toolRef.current = tool;\n> 63 |   colorRef.current = color;\n     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot update ref during render\n  64 |\n  65 |   const currentSize = tool === 'brush' ? brushSize : tool === 'eraser' ? eraserSize : penSize;\n  66 |","React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'brushSize', 'eraserSize', and 'penSize'. Either include them or remove the dependency array.",["1285"],"Error: Cannot access variable before it is declared\