 such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\DrawingEditor.tsx:573:25\n  571 |         <AnimationBar\n  572 |           frameCount={framesRef.current.length}\n> 573 |           currentFrame={currentFrameRef.current}\n      |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  574 |           fps={fpsRef.current}\n  575 |           isPlaying={isPlaying}\n  576 |           onSelectFrame={selectFrame}","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\DrawingEditor.tsx:574:16\n  572 |           frameCount={framesRef.current.length}\n  573 |           currentFrame={currentFrameRef.current}\n> 574 |           fps={fpsRef.current}\n      |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  575 |           isPlaying={isPlaying}\n  576 |           onSelectFrame={selectFrame}\n  577 |           onAddFrame={addFrame}","The ref value 'idRef.current' will likely have changed by the time this effect cleanup function runs. If this ref points to a node rendered by React, copy 'idRef.current' to a variable inside the effect, and use that variable in the cleanup function.","'smcWalk' is assigned a value but never used.","'COLS' is defined but never used.",["1286"],"'ROWS' is defined but never used.",["1287"],"'ringStackScript' is assigned a value but never used.","'WarpTarget' is defined but never used.",["1288"],"'EventCondition' is defined but never used.",["1289"],"'SpellEditor' 