Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\GameMaker.tsx:7351:67\n  7349 |                     </div>\n  7350 |                     <div className={`absolute right-0.5 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-8 h-8 pointer-events-none transition-colors rounded-r ${touchRef.current.right ? 'bg-indigo-500/30' : ''} flex items-center justify-end pr-1`}>\n> 7351 |                       <span className={`text-[8px] leading-none ${touchRef.current.right ? 'text-indigo-400' : 'text-gray-600'}`}>▶</span>\n       |                                                                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  7352 |                     </div>\n  7353 |                   </div>\n  7354 |","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\GameMaker.tsx:7367:24\n  7365 |                       </button>\n  7366 |                     </div>\n> 7367 |                   ) : (() => {\n       |                        ^^^^^^^\n> 7368 |                     let btnAActive = false; let btnALabel = \"\";\n       | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 7369 |                     let btnBActive = false; let btnBLabel = \"\";\n       …\n       | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 7429 |                     );\n       | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 7430 |                   })()}\n       | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This function accesses a ref value\n  7431 |                 </div>\n  7432 |               </div>\n  7433 |","Unused eslint-disable directive (no problems were reported from '@next/next/no-img-element').",{"range":"1325","text":"1326"},{"range":"1327","text":"1326"},{"range":"1328","text":"1326"},["1329","1330"],["1331","1332"],["1333","1334"],["1335","1336"],["1337","1338"],["1339","1340"],["1341","1342"],["1343","1344"],["1345","1346"],["1347","1348"],["1349","1350"],["1351","1352"],["1353","1354"],["1355","1356"],["1357","1358"],["1359","1360"],["1361","1362"],"React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'gameData'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["1363"],["1364"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'missSoulAttack' and 'resolveSoulAttack'. Either include them or remove the dependency array.",["1365"],["1366"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'appendLog' and 'endBattle'. Either include them or remove the dependency array.",["1367"],["1368"],["1369"],["1370"],"'findPreset' is defined but never used.",["1371"],"'onPostScore' is defined but never used.","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\HashtagView.tsx:49:21\n  47 |   }, [normalized, userId]);\n  48 |\n> 49 |   useEffect(() => { fetchPosts(); }, [fetchPosts]);\n     |                     ^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  50 |\n  51 |   const handleLike = async (id: string) => {\n  52 |     setPosts(prev => prev.map(p => p.id !== id ? p : { ...p, liked: !p.liked, likes: Math.max(0, p.liked ? p.likes - 1 : p.likes + 1) }));","'walkPresets' is defined but never used.","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\ImportDialog.tsx:24:7\n  22 |   useEffect(() => {\n  23 |     if (!open) {\n> 24 |       setImageUrl('');\n     |       ^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  25 |       setOpacity(100);\n  26 |       setSimple(false);\n  27 |       setDetected(null);",["1372"],"'index' is defined but never used.","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\LiveGameView.tsx:62:21\n  60 |   }, [userId]);\n  61 |\n> 62 |   useEffect(() => { fetchInfo(); }, [fetchInfo]);\n     |                     ^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  63 |\n  64 |   // プレイヤー位置同期 + コメントポーリング（2秒ごと）\n  65 |   useEffect(() => {","'code' is never reassigned. Use 'const' instead.",{"range":"1373","text":"1374"},"Unused eslint-disable directive (no problems were reported from 'no-new-func').",{"range":"1375","text":"1326"},["1376","1377"],"Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\MmlPlayer.tsx:21:3\n  19 |   const focusRef = useRef({ requestFocus, releaseFocus });\n  20 |   const focusRef_current = { requestFocus, releaseFocus };\n> 21 |   focusRef.current = focusRef_current;\n     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot update ref during render\n  22 |\n  23 |   useEffect(() => {\n  24 |     const el = containerRef.current;",["1378","1379"],["1380","1381"],"'openMml' is defined but never used.","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\PostContainer.tsx:564:5\n  562 |\n  563 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 564 |     setPop(true);\n      |     ^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  565 |     const timeout = setTimeout(() => setPop(false), 350);\n  566 |     return () => clearTimeout(timeout);\n  567 |   }, [index]);","'useMemo' is defined but never used.",["1382"],"Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\PostDetail.tsx:44:5\n  42 |   useEffect(() => {\n  43 |     const saved = typeof localStorage !== 'undefined' ? localStorage.getItem('unj_bbs_mode') : null;\n> 44 |     setBbsMode(saved ?? 'SNSモード');\n     |     ^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  45 |   }, []);\n  46 |\n  47 |   const [post, setPost] = useState<Post>(initial);",["1383","1384"],"Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\PostDetail.tsx:80:7\n  78 |   useEffect(() => {\n  79 |     if (replyTo) {\n> 80 |       setComposerOpen(true);\n     |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  81 |     }\n  82 |   }, [replyTo]);\n  83 |",["1385","1386"],"Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\PostDetail.tsx:628:5\n  626 |\n  627 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 628 |     setLocalPost(post);\n      |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  629 |   }, [post]);\n  630 |\n  631 |   const [menuOpen, setMenuOpen] = useState(false);","'tabs' is assigned a value but never used.","'onAddReply' is defined but never used.","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\ProfileView.tsx:55:5\n  53 |\n  54 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 55 |     setLoading(true);\n     |     ^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  56 |     const promises: Promise<any>[] = [\n  57 |       api.users.profile(slug, userId).then(data => setMyPosts(data.posts)).catch(() => setMyPosts([])),\n  58 |       api.follow.getCounts(userId).then(c => { setFollowers(c.followers); setFollowing(c.following); }).catch(() => {}),",["1387","1388"],"react-hooks/static-components","Error: Cannot create components during render\n\nComponents created during render will reset their state each time they are created. Declare components outside of render.\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\RightDrawer.tsx:155:16\n  153 |             <label className=\"text-[11px] font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider block\">プライバシー</label>\n  154 |             <div className=\"space-y-1.5\">\n> 155 |               <PrivacyToggle\n      |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This component is created during render\n  156 |                 label=\"鍵アカウント\"\n  157 |                 desc=\"フォロワーのみに投稿を公開\"\n  158 |                 icon={Lock}\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\RightDrawer.tsx:77:25\n  75 |   };\n  76 |\n> 77 |   const PrivacyToggle = ({ label, desc, icon: Icon, active, onClick }: { label: string; desc: string; icon: React.ElementType; active: boolean; onClick: () => void }) => (\n     |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 78 |     <button\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 79 |       onClick={onClick}\n     …\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 90 |     </button>\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 91 |   );\n     | ^^^^ The component is created during render here\n  92 |\n  93 |   return (\n  94 |     <>","Error: Cannot create components during render\n\nComponents created during render will reset their state each time they are created. Declare components outside of render.\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\RightDrawer.tsx:162:16\n  160 |                 onClick={() => togglePrivacy('isPrivate')}\n  161 |               />\n> 162 |               <PrivacyToggle\n      |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This component is created during render\n  163 |                 label=\"検索から除外\"\n  164 |                 desc=\"検索・トレンドに自分の投稿を出さない\"\n  165 |                 icon={EyeOff}\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\RightDrawer.tsx:77:25\n  75 |   };\n  76 |\n> 77 |   const PrivacyToggle = ({ label, desc, icon: Icon, active, onClick }: { label: string; desc: string; icon: React.ElementType; active: boolean; onClick: () => void }) => (\n     |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 78 |     <button\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 79 |       onClick={onClick}\n     …\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 90 |     </button>\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 91 |   );\n     | ^^^^ The component is created during render here\n  92 |\n  93 |   return (\n  94 |     <>","Error: Cannot create components during render\n\nComponents created during render will reset their state each time they are created. Declare components outside of render.\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\RightDrawer.tsx:169:16\n  167 |                 onClick={() => togglePrivacy('hideFromSearch')}\n  168 |               />\n> 169 |               <PrivacyToggle\n      |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This component is created during render\n  170 |                 label=\"リアクション履歴を非公開\"\n  171 |                 desc=\"いいね／ハート等の履歴を隠す\"\n  172 |                 icon={Heart}\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\RightDrawer.tsx:77:25\n  75 |   };\n  76 |\n> 77 |   const PrivacyToggle = ({ label, desc, icon: Icon, active, onClick }: { label: string; desc: string; icon: React.ElementType; active: boolean; onClick: () => void }) => (\n     |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 78 |     <button\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 79 |       onClick={onClick}\n     …\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 90 |     </button>\n     | ^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 91 |   );\n     | ^^^^ The component is created during render here\n  92 |\n  93 |   return (\n  94 |     <>","'metadataPromise' is never reassigned. Use 'const' instead.",{"range":"1389","text":"1390"},"'metadataPromise' is assigned a value but never used.",["1391","1392"],["1393","1394"],["1395","1396"],"Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\SMCAssetPanel.tsx:280:5\n  278 |     let raf = 0;\n  279 |     let cancelled = false;\n> 280 |     setError(false);\n      |     ^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  281 |\n  282 |     const sprite = metadata?.[spriteKey];\n  283 |     const anim = sprite?.animations?.[animName];",["1397","1398"],"Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Math.random` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\SpellCutscene.tsx:28:29\n  26 |   const rootRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n  27 |   const [uiScale, setUiScale] = useState(1);\n> 28 |   const idRef = useRef(`sc${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 6)}`);\n     |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  29 |   const id = idRef.current;\n  30 |\n  31 |   useLayoutEffect(() => {","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\SpellCutscene.tsx:29:14\n  27 |   const [uiScale, setUiScale] = useState(1);\n  28 |   const idRef = useRef(`sc${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 6)}`);\n> 29 |   const id = idRef.current;\n     |              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  30 |\n  31 |   useLayoutEffect(() => {\n  32 |     const el = rootRef.current;",["1399"],["1400"],["1401"],["1402"],"'toXY' is defined but never used.",["1403"],"'way' is defined but never used.",["1404"],"Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\WalkSpritePreview.tsx:40:5\n  38 |     let std: WalkStandard | null = null;\n  39 |     let cancelled = false;\n> 40 |     setError(false);\n     |     ^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  41 |\n  42 |     loadImage(url).then((loaded) => {\n  43 |       if (cancelled) return;","'encodeId' is defined but never used.",["1405"],["1406","1407"],["1408","1409"],["1410","1411"],"'_name' is defined but never used.","'_manifest' is defined but never used.",["1412","1413"],["1414","1415"],"'e' is defined but never used.",["1416","1417"],["1418","1419"],["1420","1421"],["1422","1423"],["1424","1425"],["1426","1427"],["1428","1429"],["1430","1431"],["1432","1433"],["1434","1435"],["1436","1437"],["1438","1439"],["1440","1441"],["1442","1443"],["1444","1445"],["1446","1447"],["1448","1449"],"'_ipAddress' is defined but never used.","'_gameId' is defined but never used.","'_sessionId' is defined but never used.","'_x' is defined but never used.","'_y' is defined but never used.","'_emoji' is defined but never used.","'_excludeSession' is defined but never used.",["1450","1451"],["1452","1453"],["1454","1455"],["1456"],"'nx' is never reassigned. Use 'const' instead.",{"range":"1457","text":"1458"},"'ny' is never reassigned. Use 'const' instead.",{"range":"1459","text":"1460"},"'TS' is assigned a value but never used.",["1461","1462"],["1463","1464"],["1465","1466"],["1467","1468"],["1469","1470"],["1471","1472"],["1473","1474"],"Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:65:3\n  63 |   const engineRef = useRef<Yume25DEngine | null>(null);\n  64 |   const layoutRef = useRef(layout);\n> 65 |   layoutRef.current = layout;\n     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot update ref during render\n  66 |\n  67 |   const [view, setView] = useState<'2d' | '3d'>('2d');\n  68 |   const [tool, setTool] = useState<Tool>('wall');","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:79:3\n  77 |   const idleTimerRef = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);\n  78 |   const dialogueRef = useRef<DialogueState | null>(null);\n> 79 |   dialogueRef.current = dialogue;\n     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot update ref during render\n  80 |\n  81 |   const playing = isPlaying || !!demo;\n  82 |   const is3d = playing || view === '3d';","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:129:7\n  127 |   useEffect(() => {\n  128 |     if (!playing || dialogue || demo) {\n> 129 |       setShowControlGuide(false);\n      |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  130 |       if (idleTimerRef.current) clearTimeout(idleTimerRef.current);\n  131 |       return;\n  132 |     }","Error: This value cannot be modified\n\nModifying a value used previously in an effect function or as an effect dependency is not allowed. Consider moving the modification before calling useEffect().\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:199:5\n  197 |     const inp = engineRef.current?.input;\n  198 |     if (!inp || !virtualKeys) return;\n> 199 |     inp.forward = virtualKeys.up;\n      |     ^^^ `engineRef` cannot be modified\n  200 |     inp.back = virtualKeys.down;\n  201 |     inp.strafeL = virtualKeys.left;\n  202 |     inp.strafeR = virtualKeys.right;","React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'virtualKeys'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["1475"],"Error: Cannot access variable before it is declared\n\n`handleTalk` is accessed before it is declared, which prevents the earlier access from updating when this value changes over time.\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:220:7\n  218 |   useEffect(() => {\n  219 |     if (virtualKeys?.shoot) {\n> 220 |       handleTalk();\n      |       ^^^^^^^^^^ `handleTalk` accessed before it is declared\n  221 |     }\n  222 |   }, [virtualKeys?.shoot]);\n  223 |\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:292:3\n  290 |\n  291 |   // ── 「はなす」：近くの interactive なビルボードがあれば会話ウィンドウを開く ──\n> 292 |   const handleTalk = () => {\n      |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 293 |     const b = engineRef.current?.getInteractable();\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 294 |     if (b) setDialogue({ message: b.message || '……', choices: b.choices });\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 295 |   };\n      | ^^^^^ `handleTalk` is declared here\n  296 |\n  297 |   // ── 2Dエディタ描画 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  298 |   useEffect(() => {","React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'onLayoutChange'. Either include it or remove the dependency array. If 'onLayoutChange' changes too often, find the parent component that defines it and wrap that definition in useCallback.",["1476"],"Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:239:19\n  237 |       e.preventDefault();\n  238 |       tryCapturePointer(e.currentTarget as HTMLElement, e.pointerId);\n> 239 |       const inp = engineRef.current?.input; if (inp) inp[prop] = true;\n      |                   ^^^^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  240 |     },\n  241 |     onPointerUp: () => { const inp = engineRef.current?.input; if (inp) inp[prop] = false; },\n  242 |     onPointerCancel: () => { const inp = engineRef.current?.input; if (inp) inp[prop] = false; },","Error: This value cannot be modified\n\nModifying a value used previously in an effect function or as an effect dependency is not allowed. Consider moving the modification before calling useEffect().\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:272:71\n  270 |     const dx = e.clientX - (rect.left + rect.width / 2), dy = e.clientY - (rect.top + rect.height / 2);\n  271 |     const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\n> 272 |     if (dist < PAD_DEADZONE) { inp.forward = inp.back = inp.strafeL = inp.strafeR = false; return; }\n      |                                                                       ^^^ `engineRef` cannot be modified\n  273 |     const nx = dx / dist, ny = dy / dist;\n  274 |     const AXIS = 0.35;\n  275 |     inp.strafeR = nx > AXIS; inp.strafeL = nx < -AXIS;","Error: This value cannot be modified\n\nModifying a value used previously in an effect function or as an effect dependency is not allowed. Consider moving the modification before calling useEffect().\n\nC:\\_own\\git\\_users\\onjmin\\unj-reze\\components\\Yume25DMaker.tsx:288:91\n  286 |     if (dpadPointerRef.current !== e.pointerId) return;\n  287 |     dpadPointerRef.current = null;\n> 288 |     const inp = engineRef.current?.input; if (inp) inp.forward = inp.back = inp.strafeL = inp.strafeR = false;\n      |                                                                                           ^^^ `engineRef` cannot be modified\n  289 |   };\n  290 |\n  291 |   // ── 「はなす」：近くの interactive なビルボードがあれば会話ウィンドウを開く ──","React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'playerAppearance'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["1477"],["1478"],"'React' is defined but never used.",["1479"],[593,623],"const displayPosts = [...posts];",{"kind":"1480","justification":"1481"},{"kind":"1480","justification":"1481"},{"desc":"1482","fix":"1483"},{"desc":"1484","fix":"1485"},{"messageId":"1486","data":"1487","fix":"1488","desc":"1489"},{"messageId":"1486","data":"1490","fix":"1491","desc":"1492"},{"messageId":"1486","data":"149